  PlantName: Piranha
  PlantDescription: Piranhas are freshwater fish native to South American river basins
    like the Amazon, characterized by deep, flattened bodies and razor-sharp, interlocking
    triangular teeth. Despite their fearsome reputation as aggressive man-eaters,
    they are actually omnivores that feed on fish, insects, plants, and seeds.
